---
title: Dashboard and targets
description: Read the CRM dashboard — wins, pipeline, team, business, revenue and follow-ups — and set sales targets.
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

Select **Dashboard** in the CRM workspace. The figures cover only the opportunities you can see (see [Who sees which opportunities](/en/crm/access-settings/#who-sees-which-opportunities)). Select any number to open the board filtered the same way.

At the top, choose the period — **This month**, **This quarter**, **This year** or **Custom** — and filter by PIC, service, lead type or source. **Export CSV** downloads the figures.

## How deals are counted

- **Won**, **Lost** and **Cancelled** — a deal counts in the period of its last move to that outcome.
- **Win rate** — deals won ÷ deals touched (moved) in the period. Cancelled deals are left out.
- Amounts are shown per currency; they are never converted.
- Comparisons with the previous period show as "+x% vs previous", or "no comparison" for periods before records began.

## The tabs

| Tab | What it shows |
|---|---|
| **Overview** | New opportunities, won, won value, lost, cancelled, win rate, and the weighted pipeline of open deals right now; won and lost by month. Gaps before records began mean no data, not zero. |
| **Targets** | How far the firm, the departments and each person are towards their annual or quarterly targets. |
| **Pipeline** | Deals in each stage and the average time there; the average time to win; the funnel from stage to stage; why deals did not close. |
| **Team** | Results by PIC, and by department (the PIC's current department). |
| **Business** | Results by service, source, referrer and market. A deal with two services counts under both. |
| **Revenue** | After the win: collected, invoiced but not yet paid, and not yet invoiced. A forecast of open deals for the next six months by expected close date, in full and weighted. |
| **Follow-ups** | Deals that need chasing now: **Overdue**, **Due today** and **Due soon** (next 7 days), with the stage and the number of days. |

## Set a target

**Who:** team leads and tenant admins. Only tenant admins can set targets for the whole firm or a department.

{% steps %}
1. Open **Dashboard** › **Targets** and select **Set a target**.
2. Choose whom it is for — **Whole firm**, **Department** or **Person** — and the period, **Annual** or **Quarterly**.
3. Type the amount, in the CRM currency.
4. Select **Save target**.
{% /steps %}

Progress is measured by the value won, counted as above.
